+After splitting a large script into pieces, an imported script is loaded and
+executed at the moment the importing script is sourced.  Every |:import| loads
+the imported script to find the items defined there.  However, if an imported
+script is large, then the startup time may become noticeably slower, but on
+the other hand if there are errors they will be detected at import time.
 
